{"alias":"con_290e8abfd68a4beba84e68447fb8da72","dates":{},"display_label":"Math-10858-A1","record":{"artifacts":[{"location":"in_repository","media_type":"text/markdown","path":"files/attempt.md","role":"manuscript"},{"location":"in_repository","media_type":"text/markdown","path":"files/disclosures.md","role":"supplementary"}],"attribution":{"contribution_mode":"ai_only","humans":[{"authorship_confirmation":"confirmed","display_name":"gavenren","github_id":206281466,"login_at_event":"gavenren","person_ref":"per_dbb277516a3f40f691018b44def80ced","roles":["prompting","submission"]}],"organisations":[],"submitter":{"authorship_confirmation":"confirmed","display_name":"gavenren","github_id":206281466,"login_at_event":"gavenren","person_ref":"per_dbb277516a3f40f691018b44def80ced","roles":["prompting","submission"]}},"claim":{"assumptions":[],"limitations":[],"scope_statement":"Reports the established disproof of the exact shifted coefficient-difference conjecture, credited to Katkova, Shapiro and Vishnyakova (2024), Section 5. Gives a complete self-contained proof that (x+1)^22(38x^2-188x+326) has 22 real roots counted with multiplicity but shifted parity statistic 20. Proves a closed-form family for every degree n>=24 with exactly n-2 real roots and statistic n-4; classifies the same family over 15<=n<=23; and proves that sufficiently small rational splittings give simple roots in every degree n>=24. Supplies an explicit primitive integer degree-24 polynomial with 22 distinct negative rational roots and statistic 20. Includes full exact coefficient certificates and a separate verifier with independent interpolation and Sturm computations. No historical novelty or global minimum-degree claim is made.","type":"literature_report"},"contribution_id":"con_290e8abfd68a4beba84e68447fb8da72","declarations":{"ai_disclosure":{"actor":"per_dbb277516a3f40f691018b44def80ced","confirmed":true,"evidence_url":"https://github.com/We-Solve/research/issues/23","recorded_at":"2026-10-18T1